From: fedora-opd2413 <noreply@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:57:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro: add pmic-glink
 orientation-gpios

Without orientation-gpios on pmic-glink, pmic_glink_ucsi cannot determine
the Type-C plug orientation for plain USB (non-DP Alt Mode) attachments,
leaving the QMP USB3/DP combo PHY stuck in NORMAL orientation so USB 3.x
devices only enumerate at SuperSpeed in one plug orientation and fall back
to USB 2.0 (480M) when flipped.

Probing all GPIOs on the OnePlus Pad 2 Pro with a USB 3.2 Gen 2 (10 Gbps)
NVMe enclosure in both plug orientations confirmed TLMM GPIO 61 toggles
with plug orientation: HIGH corresponds to TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE and
LOW corresponds to TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL (matching sm8750-mtp/qrd).
Declare orientation-gpios as GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH so pmic_glink_ucsi reports
TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE on HIGH and TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL on LOW.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
index 1a2b3c4d5..6f7e8d9c0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@
 			     "qcom,pmic-glink";
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
+		orientation-gpios = <&tlmm 61 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
 		connector@0 {
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
-- 
